Subject: read_text reports the row as drawn under smooth scrolling

smooth-scroll draws the viewport shifted by a sub-row offset (a gesture's
remainder, the leftover height). imePoint, clicks and selection use the rows
as drawn, but read_text's tl_px_y still gave the row-aligned position, so an
embedder couldn't tell where a row is on screen. Add the same shift.

Calm's own patch (not from thdxg/ghostty); applies on top of 0005.

diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -2099,6 +2099,12 @@

             // Add padding
             y += @floatFromInt(self.size.padding.top);
+
+            // Of the row as it is drawn: smooth scrolling draws the grid
+            // shifted by a sub-row offset, as imePoint already accounts for.
+            // Without it, an embedder placing things on the text (Calm's
+            // link marks, its cell hit-testing) lands a row off.
+            y += self.viewportPixelShift();

             // Scale
             y /= content_scale.y;
